onflict and performance concerns. We provide guidance and resources to resolve issues in an effective, thorough and timely manner. Key services provided by Staff and Faculty Relations include the following: Management and remediation of performance and misconduct concerns Collaboration with leaders to address employee relations questions and concerns Conflict Resolution Assists with questions regarding Employee Assistance Program (EAP) service referrals Workplace Investigations, including interviews with individuals to obtain a clear picture of the workplace concerns Guidance with Policy Interpretation Non-disciplinary coaching or counseling approaches Best practices in documentation Partner with leaders to address general concerns about the work environment, professionalism or collegiality within their areas Drug and Alcohol Testing Title IX For assistance, contact Staff and Faculty Relations or your HR Service Manager . Staff and Faculty Resources Staff Resources Office of Access Compliance and Education Drug Free Awareness Program Employee Assistance Program Ethics/Safety Hotline Ombuds Policies and Procedures Faculty Resources Academic Affairs/Provost Office of Access Compliance and Education Drug Free Awareness Program Employee Assistance Program Ethics/Safety Hotline Faculty Manual Ombuds Policies Affecting Faculty Drug and Alcohol Testing Drug/Alcohol Awareness Drug/Alcohol Policy Drug/Alcohol Testing Policy (PDF) Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMSCA) Pre-employment Drug Testing Acknowledgement (PDF) Testing Guidelines (PDF) Employee Training and Acknowledgement Drug Free Awareness Program Performance Concerns Staff Staff Performance Management Staff Performance Management Policy Faculty Faculty Affairs eTPR Notebook Employee Misconduct Staff Resources Discipline Policy for Covered Employees Discipline Policy for Non-Covered Employees Faculty Resources Faculty Manual Contact Us Contact Staff Relations Learning Events Training Calendar Office of 